{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","text":"Vertices","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper that adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", can own any mutable directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation as its base through this protocol and work on it without extra hashing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Vertices.Index == Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation (","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also its ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph by key, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_successors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal the unprefixed members for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. "},{"code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that vertex’s key becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":". Otherwise it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, and traps on any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for each vertex in order, then "},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for each pair"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in order. It gives the same graph and the same position for each pair."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"text":", plus O(1) per live vertex. That matches the representation’s own page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span can exceed the vertex count, because removals leave holes and a decoded graph may start at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any position. Its decoder bounds the span at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × vertexCount + 64"},{"text":" pages. Keys before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest live key cost nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows typed as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not a requirement because its return type varies by representation.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, and a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. Generic code inserts an edge by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The underscored members are for wrappers inside the library. Callers use the representations’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"generated":true}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swif